WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
A see-saw is just a long plank on a pivot.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.530
An adult sits on one end.

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.060
That end thumps down to the ground.

4
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.450
A child climbs on at the other end.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.030
The adult is three times as heavy.

6
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.280
The adult's end stays down.

7
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:20.660
So how can a child on a see-saw
balance an adult three times as heavy?

8
00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:25.070
In this mission, you'll pin down the
turning effect of a force about a pivot,

9
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.280
and the direction it turns.

10
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.160
Then you'll balance a
uniform plank on a pivot,

11
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.660
and find the weight that holds it level.

12
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: explain how the child can
balance an adult three times as heavy.
